Z||000016||pollock||02-28-2000||11:50 AM||||korn &1FST,<P>The clutch kind can get ugly too.... I have a 65 Mustang Fastback that's pretty hotrodded.  Right after i put in my powertrax locker and new BFG 265s, i went to the dragstrip.  First pass, lined up for my burnout.  Tires hooked up instantly, rear wheels hopped off the ground (wheel hop is not a Fiero phenomenon) about 30 times in 0.8 seconds.  Front ujoint and slip yoke broke, BOTH leaf springs were permanently bent THE WRONG WAY, bent my exhaust, which in turn broke one of the trim rings around my GT exhaust exits, the driveshaft bent fuel and brake lines and dented the floor pan, and the axle housing twisted so far that the shroud around the rear ujoint hit the floor pan.  <P>Moral of the story:  with new equipment, practice launching gently and work your way up.  ||||reg||9
